{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an integer array `nums` of non-negative values and an integer `k`, split `nums` into `k` non-empty **contiguous** pieces so that the **largest piece sum is as small as possible**. Return that smallest possible largest sum."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/ae890dc0-3170-4d5f-90d0-efb9078981e9.svg",
      "alt": "nums 7, 2, 5, 10, 8 split into k = 2 pieces. Splitting after 5 gives 7 + 2 + 5 = 14 and 10 + 8 = 18: the largest is 18, the best possible. With a limit of 17, greedy pieces are 7, 2, 5 (14), then 10 (adding 8 would pass 17), then 8: three pieces, too many. So 18 is the first limit that needs at most 2 pieces.",
      "width": 796,
      "height": 378,
